What did I learn this week?

This week in Math, I learned Level 3 of solving systems of linear equations using elimination. I learned that sometimes I need to multiply both equations by different numbers before I can add or subtract them to eliminate one variable.

What was challenging?

The challenging part was choosing which numbers to multiply the equations by. I also had to be careful with negative numbers because one small mistake could make my final answer wrong.

What did I practise?

I practised solving equations with two unknown variables. I had to make the coefficients match, eliminate one variable, solve for the other variable, and then substitute my answer back into an equation.

What do I want to improve?

I want to become faster at choosing the correct numbers to multiply by. I also want to make fewer mistakes with negative numbers and check my answers more carefully.
